; ==========================================================================
; Ions. Residue names are the ones used in min.ff/ions.itp.
;
; GROMACS matches these CASE-SENSITIVELY (verified against GROMACS 2025.3;
; the 2021 series matched case-insensitively instead). Both the mixed-case
; spelling used in ions.itp and the all-uppercase spelling written by gmx
; genion and by most PDB files are therefore listed below, so either form
; is recognised.
;
; U4+ is absent on purpose: the residue name U is already taken by the RNA
; entry above and the first match wins, so adding it here would only print a
; warning on every run. Uppercase RA is left out for the same reason, though
; the mixed-case Ra is fine. Both ions still simulate correctly; they are
; simply reported outside the Ion default group by make_ndx.
; ==========================================================================
; Anions
Br			Ion
Cl			Ion
F			Ion
I			Ion
; Monatomic cations
Ag			Ion
Al			Ion
Ba			Ion
Be			Ion
Ca			Ion
Cd			Ion
Ce			Ion
Co			Ion
Cr			Ion
Cs			Ion
Cu			Ion
Dy			Ion
Er			Ion
Eu			Ion
Fe			Ion
Gd			Ion
Hf			Ion
Hg			Ion
